  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Launched in April 2022, Indonesia&#x2019;s health sector transformation aims to build a more inclusive and efficient system to support long-term human capital development. 
&#x200d;
A key milestone in this journey was the signing of Implementing Regulation No. 28/2024 in July 2024, which formalised the policy direction for scaling up Indonesia&#x2019;s primary care model. Complementing this, the Ministry of Health (MoH) initiated an internal transformation to strengthen institutional capacity, focusing on human resource management, business processes, and governance.
&#x200d;
Prospera played a strategic role in this reform process helping to align government regulations with the transformation agenda and providing technical assistance to implement the primary care model. This included addressing systemic challenges such as stunting, fragmented data architecture, and workforce planning at public health clinics. Prospera also helped develop monitoring tools and strengthen the MoH central transformation office to ensure sustained reform delivery.
&#x200d;
These efforts have helped Indonesia move from policy intent to implementation, improving the coherence and effectiveness of health sector reforms. By strengthening institutional foundations and service delivery models, this work contributes to Indonesia&#x2019;s broader goal of improving population health outcomes and building a resilient health system capable of supporting economic development.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
