   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve trade processing and reduce logistics costs, the Indonesian government introduced measures aimed at strengthening its national logistics ecosystem and enhancing the efficiency of logistics services. The Australia Indonesia Partnership for Economic Development (Prospera) collaborated with the Ministry of Finance (MoF) to drive these reforms. 
&#x200d;
Prospera&#x2019;s support included supervising the design and implementation of MoF&#x2019;s performance evaluation survey of private sector users&#x2019; experiences and business costs. 
&#x200d;
To ensure MoF&#x2019;s new standards for business-to-business digital transactions were based on robust evidence, Prospera also provided an international benchmarking review of national logistics standards and technical analysis to help MoF identify which transactions needed to be standardised.
&#x200d;
As part of a broader review of the services sector, including logistics, to identify opportunities for reform, Prospera helped MoF scope ways to boost efficiency and competitiveness in logistics services. 
&#x200d;
Prospera&#x2019;s contribution supports Indonesia&#x2019;s broader goal to streamline cross-border trade and build a more efficient logistics ecosystem, which is critical to reduce trade costs, improve competitiveness, and attract investment.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
